WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.203
You know which of two sounds you
like, long before you can say why.

00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:08.382
So Auracle never asks
you to describe a sound.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:09.735
It asks you to choose.

00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:15.948
Behind every choice, it listens for the
things you hear: how bright a sound is, how

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.617
noisy, how it starts,
and how fast it moves.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:23.968
That's eighteen measurements of every patch's
sound, all from the same short phrase,

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.707
and twenty-six more of
how the patch is built.

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:32.222
Each pick is evidence: you liked this
set of measurements more than that one.

00:00:32.572 --> 00:00:34.738
Many tastes could explain one pick.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:36.842
A few picks rule most of them out.

00:00:38.057 --> 00:00:42.317
Auracle keeps every taste that still
fits, weighted by how well it fits.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.232
With every answer, that cloud of
possible tastes draws tighter.

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:49.183
And taste isn't one direction.

00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:51.820
You can love dark drones
and bright plucks.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.778
So the model keeps several lenses, and
a sound only has to please one of them.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.856
Before every duel, it
writes down a forecast.

00:01:00.856 --> 00:01:02.225
Afterwards, it checks.

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:07.766
The TRUST view shows how honest those
forecasts have been, even when the answer is:

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.767
no better than a coin flip, yet.

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:16.187
Then it searches. Evolution proposes new
patches from a grammar of modules, and your

00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:19.389
taste tilts every proposal
toward what you'll like.

00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:21.497
Thousands are heard silently.

00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:23.497
Only the best few ever reach you.

00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:29.082
You can read what it learned: a map of
every patch you've heard, the styles it

00:01:29.082 --> 00:01:31.851
found, and each direction
with its uncertainty.

00:01:33.057 --> 00:01:35.375
And when you play, it keeps listening.

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:39.157
An offer you hear, then take or
pass, counts just like a duel.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.066
Your taste, learned in the open.

00:01:42.066 --> 00:01:43.990
And it never leaves your browser.
